{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966786,"nonce":"4Gf5nTzuK9cO+YmeNWZ62Y0PAvw=","title":"Combobox/dropdown option items don't show hover bg or selected highlight until the user","message":"Open the cn::combobox (or related dropdown-style cn widgets — likely select, dropdown_menu items below the search-driven path). The dropdown content renders, layout is correct, classes are correctly registered (padding from `.cn-combobox-item` is visible on items). But:\n\n- The currently-selected row shows no `--selected` highlight even though `.cn-combobox-item--selected` is on its class list and the CSS rule applies `background: var(--selection); color: var(--accent)`.\n- Hovering an item shows no `:hover` bg.\n\nThe MOMENT the user moves the mouse at all (even by one pixel within the dropdown, even outside it), both highlights paint correctly and behave normally for the rest of that dropdown session.\n\n\n- Cache invalidation on structural subtree rebuilds — added `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(\"structural_subtree_rebuild\")` in `windowed.rs` after `process_pending_subtree_rebuilds` (mirroring the existing `had_prop_updates` gate). Verified the cache IS being invalidated. Did not fix the symptom.\n- Bumping `--selected` from `--accent-subtle` (~10% alpha in macOS, solid `#E6EEFE` in Hybrid) to `--selection` (~24% alpha) so the colour is loud enough that any pixel of it would be obviously visible. Still invisible on first open.\n- Always-in-tree dropdown via `opacity(0.0)` + `pointer_events_none()` when closed (so open/close is a Visual rebuild not Structural). Caused the dropdown not to render at all — the paint walker has an early-out at `motion_opacity \u003c= 0.001` in [`renderer/paint/motion.rs:655`](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/paint/motion.rs#L655) which skips emitting primitives entirely. So at opacity 0 the dropdown's primitives aren't in the cache, and the subsequent visual-only opacity flip didn't repopulate them. Reverted.\n- Removing the redundant inner `Stateful\u003cNoState\u003e` wrapper around the options list. Didn't change the symptom.\n\n\n`focus_text_input(\u0026search_data)` was added in [`widgets/text_input.rs`](crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input.rs#L577) and wired into the combobox trigger's open-branch. This works correctly for the search field — focus border / bg / cursor blink all appear immediately. So focus *can* be applied on the first frame post-open; the hover / selected bg problem is specifically about CSS rules whose application timing depends on the event router or `apply_stylesheet_state_styles`.\n\n\n`apply_stylesheet_state_styles` in [`renderer/stylesheet/state.rs`](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/state.rs) is gated on `router.state_fingerprint()` changing — see [`windowed.rs:5708`](crates/blinc_app/src/windowed.rs#L5708). On first open with no mouse movement, the router fingerprint hasn't changed, so the function is skipped. `apply_stylesheet_state_styles` internally calls `apply_complex_selector_styles`, which handles both state rules AND the base-rule reset for `prev_affected` nodes. For freshly-built nodes that match `:hover` complex rules (like `.cn-combobox-item:hover`), `base_styles[node_id]` is captured inside `apply_complex_selector_styles` — not inside the subtree-rebuild path.\n\nIf that capture is what makes `apply_state_styles` correctly restore the `--selected` base on every frame, then skipping `apply_stylesheet_state_styles` on the first open means the option_item's props are right ONCE (from `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree`) but get reset to a stale \"base\" on the next paint where state-styles DO run.\n\nNext debug step: instrument both `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree` and `apply_complex_selector_styles` to log the rgba of `props.background` on a `cn-combobox-item--selected` node across the open → first-mouse-move sequence. Compare to verify whether the bg is set then unset, vs never set.\n\n\n- Same symptom likely affects `cn::select` (uses `.cn-select-item--selected`) and possibly `cn::dropdown_menu` items.\n- Mouse-move workaround is accepted for now — the focus path (search input autofocus) gives the user a reason to move their mouse off the trigger naturally anyway.\n\n\n- [`crates/blinc_cn/src/components/combobox.rs`](crates/blinc_cn/src/components/combobox.rs) — combobox builder\n- [`crates/blinc_cn/src/cn_styles.rs`](crates/blinc_cn/src/cn_styles.rs#L950) — `.cn-combobox-item*` rules\n- [`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/base.rs`](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/base.rs#L345) — `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree`\n- [`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/state.rs`](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/state.rs) — `apply_stylesheet_state_styles`\n- [`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/selectors.rs`](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/selectors.rs#L364) — `apply_complex_selector_styles`\n- [`crates/blinc_app/src/windowed.rs`](crates/blinc_app/src/windowed.rs#L5708) — the `state_fingerprint` gate","files":null}]}